{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/147523-conversion-guide","id":147523,"title":"Conversion guide","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-23T21:07:13-07:00","id":147523,"title":"Conversion guide","content":"Has anyone used the conversion guide for werewolf to transfer apocalypse campaigns into nwod rules? My group greatly preferred the nwod (forsaken) combat system to that of Apocalypse, not that I blame them. Having to roll a accuracy roll, followed by a damage roll, countered by a soak roll, then the enemies 2 rolls vs your soak roll makes for a long evening. 6 turns can last a whole hell of a lot longer then intended. Knowing the Garou are great big murder machines, something about all that time taken up rolling seems... disheartening? <br /> <br /> I'd post this in the apocalypse thread but I figure this sorta topic is universal. So any success stories?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-24T10:55:28-07:00","id":147971,"title":"","content":"Nothing I've used in my game yet, but I used to have a rough sketch of converting the planetary spirits from <i>Rage Across the Heavens</i> into nWoD totems/deities/what have you. Ruatma, the Incarna of Uranus, was responsible for a bunch of mystery cults; Pluto was going to be something death/Underworld-related.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-24T14:37:35-07:00","id":148142,"title":"","content":"I mostly just don't want to throw two sets of rules at people in a short period of time. Though I do like the brutality of the apocalypse damaging strikes, it also brings monotony on the higher soak bosses<br /> <br /> What if I didn't want to bring apocalypse into forsaken's world but just use the rules? Could I get away with just sliding in the combat rules? Or is it more involved then that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":1939,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","user":"Lyrics Of War","date":". 05-24-2014, 06:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}